window.EN={"1":"Having defeated the Djute tribe, the strongest tribe on the plain,","2":"Roy's Etrurian army now closes in on Bulgar, the largest city on the Sacae plain.","3":"Bulgar developed as a crossroads of transportation and commerce linking the three regions of Etruria, Bern, and Ilia,","4":"and had thrived as a free city, but with Bern's recent invasion, that history came to an end,","5":"and now former Etrurian prime minister Roartz governs this land under Bern's protection.","6":"To take Sacae back from Bern's hands, and to use it as a foothold for an advance into Bern,","7":"Roy and the others now advance their army toward that land.","8":"Ngh... So they've finally come. And so much sooner than I thought...","9":"At this rate, there's no way to prepare to fight!","10":"We will hold off the enemy.","11":"You should remain inside the manor and prepare to meet them there.","12":"...Do we have any chance of winning?","13":"We won't know until we try.","14":"If we don't even know whether we can win...","15":"Then what will you do? Will you run away from here too?","16":"Where is there for you to go now?","17":"Ugh...","18":"Since I've received Lady Brunya's order to protect you,","19":"I will guard you with everything I have.","20":"So you too must resolve yourself to fight!","21":"Nngh... A-alright, I understand.","22":"Then I'll leave what's outside to you.","23":"...That man is the prime minister of Etruria?","24":"Are we really fighting for a man like that?","25":"Don't say that.","26":"Lady Brunya didn't tell us to protect that man out of any gladness either.","27":"...As warriors, we need only think about fulfilling our duty.","28":"......","29":"There's also word that a faction of the \"Grey Wolves\" has slipped into this city of Bulgar.","30":"Don't let your guard down.","31":"Yessir.","32":"Princess Guinivere.","33":"Lord Roy... Another battle is about to begin today, isn't it.","34":"Yes. I'm sorry I haven't been able to find the time to properly talk with you...","35":"I apologize.","36":"No, not at all. After all, the real cause of all this is my brother.","37":"Princess Guinivere.","38":"...Yes.","39":"May I ask you the reason?","40":"The reason King Zephiel was nearly assassinated by his own father...","41":"...My brother and I had different mothers. We're half-siblings.","42":"I heard King Zephiel's mother was an Etrurian princess?","43":"Yes. She became my father's consort to strengthen the bond between Etruria and Bern.","44":"But my father already had a woman he loved by then — and that woman is my mother.","45":"......","46":"The marriage between my father and my brother's mother—","47":"—was apparently forced through by the people around him, the other nobles and his chief vassals.","48":"Because of that, my father didn't love my brother's mother, and he seems to have come to find my brother tiresome.","49":"Is that why the relationship between the former king of Bern and King Zephiel turned sour?","50":"No. Even so, my brother apparently tried desperately to earn our father's favor.","51":"He trained himself in the knowledge and refinement needed to inherit the throne, and in the military discipline needed to lead an army...","52":"My brother grew into a prince fit in every way to inherit the kingdom of Bern.","53":"But then, why did the former king of Bern...","54":"Lord Roy! Preparations for the attack are complete!","55":"Understood, I'll go right away!","56":"Princess Guinivere, I'm sorry, but...","57":"No, please — do take care...","58":"Well, well, it's finally started, hasn't it.","59":"...So it seems.","60":"Just when I thought Bern had finished attacking, now it's Etruria.","61":"Honestly, I wish they'd give us a break.","62":"......","63":"Can't be helped, I suppose. This town is a crossroads, after all.","64":"Everyone's bound to want it... ...there we go.","65":"H-hey, old woman, where are you off to?","66":"Off to watch the battle.","67":"To see the skill of this rumored general called Roy.","68":"S-such a carefree thing to be doing...!","69":"Oh, don't worry, don't worry...","70":"Hey, wait a second — where are you off to too, old man!","71":"The reinforcements should be arriving soon.","72":"Hey—","73":"Open the front gate and bring the reinforcements into the town.","74":"Yessir.","75":"Should be about time... Alright, opening the gate!","76":"Tell the ones hiding in the town to join the attack.","77":"Yes.","78":"Before the war, I used to sell all sorts of weapons to the Bern army...","79":"But if this place gets occupied, those guys won't pay up at all.","80":"This one's fine on credit, so do something about it, would you.","81":"I kept this Dragonkiller hidden from the Bern lot.","82":"If they'd found it, it would've been confiscated on the spot.","83":"You get why, don't you?","84":"How about a magic ring from Etruria?","85":"Up until not long ago, saying that would get me a lot of buyers, but...","86":"With the war on, I had no choice but to close up shop.","87":"I'll give you one — it's not like it'll sell anyway...","88":"Heave... ho...","89":"It fell on the battlefield, so it's not stealing, right?","90":"With this, I bet I could sell it for a lot—","91":"Waah! A-a person from Bern?","92":"Huh? What's this sword? I dunno.","93":"Welp.","94":"This is a lucky goddess statue.","95":"Come to think of it, travelers used to get completely fooled by it, but...","96":"With this war on, I can't even do business.","97":"If you want it, take it — it's not like luck's coming our way anyway.","98":"This is Sacae's pride, the longbow — want to take it with you?","99":"You don't owe me anything for it. Just do something about those Bern guys for me instead.","100":"Drive them out of Bulgar.","101":"My name is Kell.","102":"My final sword... Bear witness.","103":"As one who bears a sword, this too was inevitable...","104":"Ho ho ho, you're quite capable, aren't you.","105":"Wh-who are you?","106":"Hey, wait! You can't just walk in! General Roy is busy!","107":"What's going on?","108":"Sir! This person keeps insisting on meeting with General Roy.","109":"We tried to send her away since you're busy, but—","110":"Wouldn't it not be too late, even after hearing what I have to say?","111":"I think I've brought a story that would interest even you.","112":"An interesting story?","113":"It concerns a creature that takes a human's form, but isn't human.","114":"...I'll talk with this person for a while.","115":"The rest of you, please keep watch at the entrance to the room.","116":"Yessir.","117":"Ho ho, your face just changed color.","118":"Old woman, do you mean that creature is possibly—","119":"I mean the \"dragons.\"","120":"The \"dragons\" you're talking about—","121":"You don't mean the wyverns that dragon knights ride, but rather... something among Bern's soldiers themselves?","122":"Yes, that's it.","123":"Those are the \"dragons\" that should have perished in that Human-Dragon War, long ago.","124":"!? Just who are you...?","125":"I am one called Niime.","126":"Perhaps because I study ancient dark magic deep in the mountains, I'm sometimes called the \"Mountain Hermit.\"","127":"At first I thought this whole uproar was just an ordinary war, and watched it from the sidelines, but—","128":"It seems something ominous is mixed in among the soldiers.","129":"Curious, I looked into it.","130":"And did you find out anything?","131":"Hmm, well — there are too many mysteries about the \"dragons.\" I tried poring over various old texts, but—","132":"There weren't many records that could shed light on it. Except...","133":"...Except?","134":"I've come to think they may have revived the \"Demon Dragon.\"","135":"The \"Demon Dragon\"... you mean the dragon chieftain said to have been slain by the hero Hartmut?","136":"That's right.","137":"The \"dragons\" are creatures overwhelmingly superior to humans — in vitality, in intelligence...","138":"But it seems their power to bear children — to increase their numbers — was decisively inferior to humans'.","139":"But among them, only the \"Demon Dragon\" is said to have had the power to create more \"dragons.\"","140":"I'm fairly certain I've seen that in an old document.","141":"Such power...","142":"A being capable of creating \"dragons\"—","143":"Hasn't Bern revived it, and gotten hold of a \"dragon\" through it, I wonder.","144":"That may well be so.","145":"Now then, I have a proposal.","146":"Perhaps because I pursue ancient magic, I want to solve more of the mysteries surrounding the \"dragons.\"","147":"Would you allow me to accompany you and the others?","148":"I can use dark magic, I believe I'd be of use.","149":"...Understood.","150":"When it comes to the \"dragons,\" there's a lot we want to know too.","151":"There may be danger involved, but if you're still willing, let's go together."};
